---
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Linear Algebra Notes | Engineering Mathematics | ACEgate ECE"
  description="Complete Linear Algebra notes for GATE ECE preparation by ACEgate ECE."
>
  <main class="notes-page">
    <section class="notes-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <a
          href="/courses/engineering-mathematics/linear-algebra"
          class="back-link"
        >
          ← Back to Linear Algebra
        </a>

        <p class="eyebrow">Engineering Mathematics</p>

        <h1>Linear Algebra Notes</h1>

        <p class="notes-description">
          Structured Linear Algebra notes for GATE ECE preparation,
          covering important concepts, formulas and exam-oriented topics.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="notes-content">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="content-layout">
          <aside class="sidebar">
            <h2>Contents</h2>

            <nav>
              <a href="#matrices">Matrices</a>
              <a href="#determinants">Determinants</a>
              <a href="#rank">Rank of Matrix</a>
              <a href="#linear-equations">
                System of Linear Equations
              </a>
              <a href="#eigenvalues">
                Eigenvalues & Eigenvectors
              </a>
              <a href="#diagonalization">Diagonalization</a>
            </nav>
          </aside>

          <article class="notes-article">
            <section id="matrices" class="notes-section">
              <span class="section-number">01</span>
              <h2>Matrices</h2>

              <p>
                A matrix is a rectangular arrangement of numbers or
                mathematical quantities organized into rows and columns.
              </p>

              <h3>Important Concepts</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>Order of a matrix</li>
                <li>Row and column matrices</li>
                <li>Square matrices</li>
                <li>Diagonal and identity matrices</li>
                <li>Symmetric and skew-symmetric matrices</li>
                <li>Matrix addition and multiplication</li>
                <li>Transpose of a matrix</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="determinants" class="notes-section">
              <span class="section-number">02</span>
              <h2>Determinants</h2>

              <p>
                Determinants are scalar quantities associated with square
                matrices and are important in solving systems of equations
                and studying matrix properties.
              </p>

              <h3>Important Concepts</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>Determinant of a matrix</li>
                <li>Properties of determinants</li>
                <li>Minors and cofactors</li>
                <li>Expansion of determinants</li>
                <li>Singular and non-singular matrices</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="rank" class="notes-section">
              <span class="section-number">03</span>
              <h2>Rank of Matrix</h2>

              <p>
                The rank of a matrix represents the maximum number of
                linearly independent rows or columns.
              </p>

              <h3>Important Concepts</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>Rank using row reduction</li>
                <li>Elementary row operations</li>
                <li>Row echelon form</li>
                <li>Rank and linear independence</li>
                <li>Rank of a system of equations</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="linear-equations" class="notes-section">
              <span class="section-number">04</span>
              <h2>System of Linear Equations</h2>

              <p>
                Systems of linear equations can be represented using
                matrices and solved using systematic algebraic methods.
              </p>

              <h3>Important Concepts</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>Homogeneous equations</li>
                <li>Non-homogeneous equations</li>
                <li>Consistency of equations</li>
                <li>Unique solution</li>
                <li>Infinite solutions</li>
                <li>No solution</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="eigenvalues" class="notes-section">
              <span class="section-number">05</span>
              <h2>Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors</h2>

              <p>
                Eigenvalues and eigenvectors describe important properties
                of a square matrix and are frequently used in engineering
                mathematics.
              </p>

              <h3>Important Concepts</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>Characteristic equation</li>
                <li>Eigenvalues</li>
                <li>Eigenvectors</li>
                <li>Properties of eigenvalues</li>
                <li>Algebraic and geometric multiplicity</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="diagonalization" class="notes-section">
              <span class="section-number">06</span>
              <h2>Diagonalization</h2>

              <p>
                Diagonalization transforms a suitable square matrix into
                a diagonal matrix using its eigenvalues and eigenvectors.
              </p>

              <h3>Important Concepts</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>Diagonal matrix</li>
                <li>Similar matrices</li>
                <li>Diagonalization condition</li>
                <li>Eigenvector matrix</li>
                <li>Applications of diagonalization</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <div class="coming-box">
              <strong>More GATE-focused content coming soon.</strong>
              <p>
                Detailed formulas, solved examples, shortcuts and
                previous-year questions will be added here.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .notes-page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: #f8fafc;
  }

  .notes-hero {
    padding: 70px 20px 55px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a, #1e3a8a);
    color: white;
  }

  .container {
    width: min(1100px, 100%);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    color: #bfdbfe;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: white;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: #93c5fd;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .notes-description {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    color: #dbeafe;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .notes-content {
    padding: 60px 20px;
  }

  .content-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 250px 1fr;
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .sidebar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 100px;
    padding: 24px;
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
  }

  .sidebar h2 {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: #0f172a;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .sidebar nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .sidebar nav a {
    padding: 9px 10px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #475569;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .sidebar nav a:hover {
    background: #eff6ff;
    color: #2563eb;
  }

  .notes-article {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 35px;
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    border-radius: 18px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
  }

  .notes-section {
    scroll-margin-top: 100px;
    padding: 10px 0 45px;
    margin-bottom: 45px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
  }

  .section-number {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: #2563eb;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .notes-section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: #0f172a;
    font-size: 1.8rem;
  }

  .notes-section h3 {
    margin: 25px 0 12px;
    color: #1e293b;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .notes-section p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #475569;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .notes-section ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
    color: #475569;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .coming-box {
    padding: 22px;
    background: #eff6ff;
    border: 1px solid #bfdbfe;
    border-radius: 14px;
  }

  .coming-box strong {
    color: #1e3a8a;
  }

  .coming-box p {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    color: #475569;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .content-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .sidebar {
      position: static;
    }

    .sidebar nav {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .notes-article {
      padding: 25px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .notes-hero {
      padding: 50px 18px 40px;
    }

    .notes-content {
      padding: 45px 18px;
    }

    .sidebar nav {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .notes-article {
      padding: 20px;
    }

    .notes-section h2 {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>